WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.688
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.990
TOM SHAFER: We left for
college in the fall of '77.

00:00:05.990 --> 00:00:09.770
The school was well-known
for the business education

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.220
that it had at that time.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.870
And it was really emerging as
a leader in thought process

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:17.038
about kind of an independence.

00:00:17.038 --> 00:00:18.455
The liberal arts
experience that I

00:00:18.455 --> 00:00:20.540
had was very
important to beginning

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.120
to discover both
the world around you

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.600
and yourself a little bit.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:29.270
So I think, for me, it was a
real appreciation for areas

00:00:29.270 --> 00:00:32.689
that I don't know that I would
have taken myself to had I not

00:00:32.689 --> 00:00:35.960
had opportunity to
go to Hillsdale.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.120
I met my wife there.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.660
We were engaged my senior year.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.540
Mary and I both have just
great memories of our time

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:42.710
together at Hillsdale.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:44.700
It's the people that
you always remember--

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:48.080
your professors that had an
impact on you, your friends.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.330
It was just to me a
magical experience.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.150
I was engaged when I
came out of college,

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.640
got married right away, started
in the banking business.

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:56.630
It was 1981.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.160
The economy was a wreck.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:01.700
I have been basically with
three companies during that time

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:02.390
period.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:05.209
I had an opportunity to work for
people that I had respect for,

00:01:05.209 --> 00:01:07.970
people that gave
me opportunities.

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:11.570
For the last decade or so,
I've been either a president

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:13.920
or a CEO in the
banking business.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:16.370
The company we're with today
is headquartered in Detroit,

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:18.650
having merged
Chemical Bank and TCF.

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:21.800
The last merger was my
26th merger or acquisition.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.710
The industry's just been
changing at the light of speed.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:26.040
It's going to continue.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.550
So while I spend a tremendous
amount of time in the banking

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:30.920
business, I spent a
significant lot of time

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:33.580
in organizational development.

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.590
I'm incredibly honored to be
receiving the Distinguished

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:37.470
Alumni Award.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:38.750
I had a great career there.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.322
I've got lifelong
friends from there.

00:01:40.322 --> 00:01:41.780
I went to school
with people that I

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.000
have so much respect for
that have done things

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.920
that I think
completely eclipse what

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.300
I've done during my career.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:50.570
But I'm truly proud of my
association with Hillsdale,

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:53.900
honored to receive this
award, and will cherish it.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:57.250
[MUSIC PLAYING]

